-- Refinement types (widening slice 12, §2.14). `cap no_panic`'s division-
-- safety check (lib/refinecheck/division_safety.ml) is a second, specialized
-- Refine.discharge consumer alongside the general precondition/postcondition
-- pass (accept/t75, t76). It is a hybrid: a fast syntactic matcher handles
-- common divisor shapes (`_ != 0`, `_ > 0`, ...) without invoking Z3 at all;
-- `{Int | _ != 0}` matches directly, so `a / d` is approved inside the
-- `cap no_panic` module -- proving the ONE live predicate-discharge path
-- that actually gates panic-freedom (not just exhaustiveness, which
-- core-march-types.md §2.8.11 already covers). Reject companion: reject/t73
-- (`{Int | _ >= 0}`, a real but insufficient predicate).
mod SafeDiv do
  needs IO.Console
  cap no_panic
  fn safe_div(a : Int, d : {Int | _ != 0}) : Int do a / d end
  fn main() do
    println(int_to_string(safe_div(10, 2)))
  end
end
